.TH TUI_FIELDSET_INIT 3 2026-10-03 "libtuikit 0.1" "libtuikit Manual"
.SH NAME
tui_fieldset_init, tui_fieldset_free, tui_field_text, tui_field_choice,
tui_fieldset_focus, tui_fieldset_set_error, tui_fieldset_update_completion,
tui_fieldset_handle, tui_fieldset_render \- a form of several fields with
completion and validation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <tuikit/fieldset.h>
.PP
.BI "void tui_field_text(tui_field *" fl ", const char *" label ,
.BI "                         char *" buf ", size_t " size ", const char *" initial );
.BI "void tui_field_choice(tui_field *" fl ", const char *" label ,
.BI "                           const char *const *" choices ", int " n ", int " selected );
.BI "void tui_fieldset_init(tui_fieldset *" f ", tui_field *" fields ", int " n );
.BI "void tui_fieldset_free(tui_fieldset *" f );
.BI "void tui_fieldset_focus(tui_fieldset *" f ", int " i );
.BI "void tui_fieldset_set_error(tui_fieldset *" f ", const char *" msg );
.BI "void tui_fieldset_update_completion(tui_fieldset *" f );
.BI "tui_dialog_state tui_fieldset_handle(tui_fieldset *" f ", const tui_event *" ev );
.BI "int  tui_fieldset_render(tui_fieldset *" f ", tui_canvas " c );
.PP
.BI "typedef int (*tui_complete_fn)(void *" user ", int " field ", const char *" token ,
.BI "                               tui_completion *" out ", int " max );
.BI "typedef int (*tui_fieldset_validate_fn)(void *" user ", const tui_fieldset *" f ,
.BI "                                    char *" err ", size_t " errsz );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
A form edits several fields: the shape of email-cli's compose dialog
(To, Cc, Bcc, Subject, Attach, with an address drop-down) and of
issue-manager's new and edit form (title, description, type, priority,
implementer).
Like a dialog it neither blocks nor reads the terminal.
The program sees every event first, so behaviour that belongs to it \(em
what a separator key does, removing an attachment, checking a file \(em it
handles before passing the event on.
.PP
The fields are an array the caller owns.
.BR tui_field_text ()
makes a text field editing
.I buf
with a
.BR tui_lineedit_init (3)
editor;
.BR tui_field_choice ()
a field that is one of
.I n
.I choices
(not copied), changed with Left, Right and Space.
.BR tui_fieldset_init ()
puts them in a form, the focus on the first; the members
.I validate
and
.I user
and the styles may be set afterwards.
.SS Completion
A text field with
.I complete
set offers completions.
After every edit the form takes the token being typed \(em the text from
the last of the field's
.I separators
before the cursor (or from the start, when there are none), leading
spaces skipped \(em and asks
.I complete
for candidates.
When there are any, a drop-down lists them under the field
.RI ( label
shown, or
.I text
when there is no label).
The drop-down opens with nothing chosen
.RI ( cand_sel
is \-1): Down moves onto the candidates and Up back \(em from the first
one, into the field again.
Enter replaces the token with the chosen candidate's
.IR text ;
with none chosen it is the form's Enter.
Tab replaces the token with the longest prefix that all candidates share,
when that is longer than the token, and stays in the field.
Shift-Tab plays no part in completion.
Esc closes the drop-down and keeps the text; typing opens it again.
(Up to 0.3, as in email-cli, the first candidate was chosen at once and
Tab accepted it; the workspace's owner replaced that rule in 0.4.)
.BR tui_fieldset_update_completion ()
asks again, for a program that changed the text itself.
.SS Keys
Without a drop-down, Tab and Down move to the next field, Shift-Tab and Up
to the previous one (both wrap); Enter submits; Esc and Ctrl-C cancel
.RB ( TUI_DIALOG_CANCELLED ).
On submit the form calls
.IR validate :
\-1 lets it close
.RB ( TUI_DIALOG_OK );
an index puts the focus on that field and shows the message written into
.I err
under the fields \(em email-cli's "To: is empty" check.
Typing in a field clears the message;
.BR tui_fieldset_set_error ()
sets or clears it directly.
Every other key goes to the focused text field's editor.
.SS Drawing
.BR tui_fieldset_render ()
draws from the top of a canvas: a row per field with the labels in a
column (by default the focused label in
.BR TUI_STYLE_ACCENT ,
the others plain, the chosen candidate in
.BR TUI_STYLE_SELECTION ,
the message in
.BR TUI_STYLE_ERROR ),
the value
after them \(em a choice field shows "< value >" while focused \(em the
drop-down under the focused field, then the message.
It puts the terminal cursor in a focused text field, hides it otherwise,
and returns the rows used, so the program can draw what it adds (a list
of attachments) below.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR tui_fieldset_handle ()
returns the state after the event; events after the form closed are
ignored.
.BR tui_fieldset_render ()
returns the number of rows drawn.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tui_lineedit_init (3),
